---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Adeptus Mechanicus Beginner's Guide — Warhammer 40k"
  description="New to the Adeptus Mechanicus? Learn the Machine God lore, how the tech-priest army plays, how to paint red robes and metal, and what to buy first."
>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="px-6 pt-16 pb-12 border-b border-[#2a2a35]">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <a href="/factions/" class="text-sm text-[#4a4855] hover:text-[#8a8590] transition-colors mb-6 inline-block">
        ← All Factions
      </a>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-6">
        <div class="text-6xl">⚙️</div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-[#c9a84c] text-sm font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase mb-2 font-display">Faction Guide</p>
          <h1 class="font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mb-4">Adeptus Mechanicus</h1>
          <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-lg max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
            Humanity's tech-priests — half-human, half-machine, and convinced that 
            flesh is a design flaw. They worship technology as a religion, 
            replace their bodies with cybernetics until little human remains, 
            and guard the ancient knowledge of a golden age they're desperate to reclaim. 
            The most unique looking army in the game.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Quick stats -->
      <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3">
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Playstyle</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm">Shooting + Combo</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Painting</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm text-yellow-400">Medium</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Rules</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm text-red-400">Complex</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Starter Cost</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm">~$160–$240</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Lore -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-6">Who are the Adeptus Mechanicus?</h2>
      <div class="text-[#b8b4c0] leading-relaxed space-y-4 text-lg">
        <p>
          Before the Imperium existed, Mars had already built a civilization. 
          The Cult Mechanicus — the priesthood of the Machine God — 
          had been worshipping technology as religion for thousands of years 
          while Terra tore itself apart in nuclear war. 
          When the Emperor unified humanity, he needed Mars's weapons factories. 
          Mars needed Terra's armies. They signed a treaty. 
          The arrangement has never been entirely comfortable.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Mechanicus believe in the <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Omnissiah</strong> — 
          the Machine God, the divine intelligence behind all technology. 
          They believe the Emperor is a physical manifestation of this god 
          (a claim the rest of the Imperium finds deeply heretical). 
          Knowledge is sacred. Ignorance is sin. 
          Destroying working technology, even enemy technology, 
          is an act of almost religious offense.
        </p>
        <p>
          Their defining obsession is the <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">STC</strong> — 
          Standard Template Construct — an ancient database from humanity's golden age 
          containing blueprints for every machine ever devised. 
          Most STCs were lost in the Age of Strife. 
          Finding even a fragment of an STC is the greatest possible discovery. 
          Tech-Priests have started wars over a single blueprint.
        </p>
        <p>
          A Tech-Priest's spiritual journey is one of progressive augmentation. 
          They replace flesh with machine — one eye for an optical mechadendrite, 
          one arm for a servo-arm, the nervous system for hard-wired circuitry. 
          The highest-ranking Tech-Priests are barely recognizable as human. 
          The Fabricator-General of Mars is, effectively, a machine that remembers being a person. 
          This is considered the highest possible honor.
        </p>
        <p class="italic text-[#8a8590]">
          "Flesh is weak. The Machine is eternal."
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Forge Worlds -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">Choose your Forge World</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-8 text-lg">
        Forge Worlds are the AdMech equivalent of Space Marine Chapters — 
        industrial planets with distinct doctrines, colors, and battlefield approaches.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-4">
        {[
          {
            name: 'Mars',
            colors: 'Red & Silver',
            swatch1: 'bg-red-700',
            swatch2: 'bg-slate-400',
            painting: 'Medium',
            paintColor: 'text-yellow-400',
            desc: "The original Forge World. Canonical red robes and silver metal — the scheme GW uses for all their official photography. Bold and striking. Medium difficulty because red requires layering to look good but it's the most supported scheme.",
          },
          {
            name: 'Lucius',
            colors: 'Silver & White',
            swatch1: 'bg-slate-300',
            swatch2: 'bg-gray-100',
            painting: 'Medium',
            paintColor: 'text-yellow-400',
            desc: 'The Forge World of illusions — known for dimensional shielding technology and a silver/white color scheme. Elegant and clean. The cool contrast to Mars\'s warmth.',
          },
          {
            name: 'Graia',
            colors: 'Blue & Silver',
            swatch1: 'bg-blue-800',
            swatch2: 'bg-slate-400',
            painting: 'Easy',
            paintColor: 'text-green-400',
            desc: 'Dark blue robes with silver metal — one of the easiest AdMech schemes to execute. Less common on the table than Mars, which makes it stand out. Mechanicus Standard Grey spray + wash gets you most of the way there.',
          },
          {
            name: 'Stygies VIII',
            colors: 'Dark Brown & Bronze',
            swatch1: 'bg-amber-900',
            swatch2: 'bg-yellow-600',
            painting: 'Easy',
            paintColor: 'text-green-400',
            desc: "Secretive, distrusted by other Forge Worlds, suspected of xenos contact. Dark, muted brown robes with bronze metal accents. Fast to paint with contrast paints and very atmospheric on the table.",
          },
        ].map(fw => (
          <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
            <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
              <div class="flex gap-1 flex-shrink-0">
                <div class={`w-3 h-12 rounded-l ${fw.swatch1}`}></div>
                <div class={`w-3 h-12 rounded-r ${fw.swatch2}`}></div>
              </div>
              <div class="flex-1">
                <div class="flex items-center flex-wrap gap-3 mb-1">
                  <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-lg">{fw.name}</h3>
                  <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">{fw.colors}</span>
                  <span class={`text-xs font-semibold ${fw.paintColor}`}>Painting: {fw.painting}</span>
                </div>
                <p class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm leading-relaxed">{fw.desc}</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Playstyle -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-6">How they play on the table</h2>
      <div class="text-[#b8b4c0] leading-relaxed space-y-4 text-lg mb-10">
        <p>
          AdMech are a <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">mid-range shooting army</strong> 
          with a uniquely combo-driven playstyle. 
          Individual units are specialist tools — 
          Skitarii Rangers are reliable long-range shooters, 
          Sicarian Infiltrators are fast melee assassins, 
          Kastelan Robots are walking fortresses when properly supported. 
          The army rewards knowing exactly what each unit does and deploying them 
          against the right targets.
        </p>
        <p>
          The defining mechanic is <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Doctrina Imperatives</strong> — 
          special combat protocols you cycle through each turn. 
          In Protector Doctrina your Skitarii shoot better. 
          In Conqueror Doctrina they fight better in melee. 
          You can only use each a limited number of times, 
          so you're constantly thinking several turns ahead about when to switch modes. 
          It's the most tactical faction in the game for people who like planning.
        </p>
        <p>
          The unit roster is strikingly varied: Skitarii infantry, walking spider-legged tanks (Dunecrawlers), 
          bipedal strider vehicles (Ironstriders), ancient giant robots (Kastelans), 
          tracked cannon platforms with human torsos (Kataphrons). 
          Few armies have this much visual variety, and painting the collection feels like 
          a genuinely diverse project rather than repetitive squads.
        </p>
        <p>
          Honest caveat: <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">this is not a beginner army</strong>. 
          The synergies between units matter a lot, mistakes are punishing, 
          and the Doctrina system adds planning overhead on top of learning the base rules. 
          If you're drawn to the aesthetic and lore, play a few games with a friend first 
          before committing. If you love puzzle-solving, this is your faction.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-3 text-green-400">AdMech are for you if...</h3>
          <ul class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm space-y-2">
            <li>✓ The half-human, half-machine aesthetic is exactly what you want</li>
            <li>✓ You like puzzle-solving and planning multiple turns ahead</li>
            <li>✓ You want the most unique looking army in the game</li>
            <li>✓ You enjoy painting a huge variety of model types</li>
            <li>✓ You're interested in the tech-religion lore angle</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-3 text-red-400">Maybe look elsewhere if...</h3>
          <ul class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm space-y-2">
            <li>✗ You're new to 40k — too many synergies to manage early</li>
            <li>✗ You want a simple, forgiving playstyle</li>
            <li>✗ You prefer organic, living aesthetics</li>
            <li>✗ You want a horde army with lots of bodies</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Painting -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">How to paint Adeptus Mechanicus</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-4 text-lg">Mars scheme (red + silver). The canonical look, and the one with the most tutorials.</p>
      <p class="text-[#b8b4c0] mb-10 leading-relaxed">
        AdMech models have two distinct surfaces: flowing fabric robes and intricate mechanical parts. 
        Each requires a different approach. The good news is that both are relatively straightforward 
        — red robes with a wash look immediately striking, and metallic washes do most of the work 
        on the mechanical components. The challenge is the sheer density of tiny detail per model.
      </p>

      <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold mb-4 text-[#f0ede8]">The robes</h3>
      <div class="space-y-3 mb-8">
        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">1</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Spray Mephiston Red</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">The base coat over everything. Full coverage is important — red over black primer looks muddy and is harder to fix than starting light.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">2</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Agrax Earthshade wash over all fabric</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">A generous wash into all the robe folds. It darkens the recesses and gives the fabric genuine depth — takes the red from flat to rich.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">3</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Evil Sunz Scarlet layer on raised folds</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Restore the brighter red on the raised areas of the robes, avoiding the recesses. This creates the classic shaded fabric look without advanced techniques.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold mb-4 text-[#f0ede8]">The mechanical parts</h3>
      <div class="space-y-3 mb-8">
        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">4</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Leadbelcher on all metal surfaces</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Cybernetic limbs, exposed pistons, weapon casings, tubes, cables. AdMech models have a lot of metal — drybrush it liberally.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">5</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Nuln Oil wash over all metal</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Gets into every cable groove, every rivet, every gear tooth. The single most effective step on mechanical models — the metal goes from flat to industrial instantly.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">6</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Drybrush Ironbreaker on raised metal edges</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Brings the metallic sheen back on corners and raised surfaces. Makes the machinery look like it's actually used — worn edges, maintained metal.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold mb-4 text-[#f0ede8]">The finishing details</h3>
      <div class="space-y-3 mb-8">
        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">7</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Corax White on skull faces and bone details</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Many Tech-Priests have exposed or augmetic skulls. A clean white over these — then a thin wash of Agrax Earthshade to age them — creates the perfect bleached bone look.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">8</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Tesseract Glow or Moot Green on optical lenses</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Every AdMech model has optical sensors, augmetic eyes, or weapon targeting lenses. A tiny dab of glowing green makes them read as powered up and alive. This one detail sells the whole model.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#c9a84c] rounded-lg p-5">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-2">Patience over speed</h3>
        <p class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm leading-relaxed">
          AdMech models have more detail per model than almost anything else in the game. 
          Don't rush. Work in good light with magnification if you have it. 
          A single well-painted Tech-Priest Dominus is a showpiece. 
          The army is smaller than most (fewer models overall), 
          so you can afford to spend more time on each one — and it shows.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- What to buy -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">What to buy first</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-10 text-lg">One box. It will take longer to assemble than you expect. That's the AdMech experience — and it's worth it.</p>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#c9a84c] rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <div class="mb-4">
          <span class="bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] text-xs font-semibold px-2 py-0.5 rounded font-display mr-2">Start Here</span>
          <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">~$160</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-2">Combat Patrol: Adeptus Mechanicus</h3>
        <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          Includes a Tech-Priest Manipulus (your commander), 10 Skitarii Vanguard or Rangers 
          (core infantry), 5 Pteraxii Sterylizors or Skystalkers (fast flying assault troops), 
          and 3 Serberys Sulphurhounds or Raiders (fast cavalry). A surprisingly mobile 
          force with huge build variety — every kit builds two different units.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0CNTTMBPD?tag=grimdarkprime-20"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="inline-block bg-[#c9a84c] hover:bg-[#dfc070] text-[#111113] font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded text-sm transition-colors font-display"
        >
          See price on Amazon →
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <div class="mb-3">
          <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">~$75 · the natural second purchase</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-2">Kastelan Robots</h3>
        <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          Two enormous ancient robots controlled by a Datasmith Tech-Priest. 
          Pre-Imperial machines that the Mechanicus maintains but cannot fully understand — 
          which delights them. Extremely durable and powerful when buffed correctly, 
          they're one of the faction's most unique tactical elements 
          and absolutely spectacular models to paint.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=kastelan+robots+adeptus+mechanicus+warhammer&tag=grimdarkprime-20"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="inline-block border border-[#2a2a35] hover:border-[#c9a84c] text-[#b8b4c0] hover:text-[#c9a84c] font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded text-sm transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Search Amazon →
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- Paints -->
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-6">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-4">Paints you need (Mars scheme)</h3>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          {[
            { name: 'Mephiston Red Spray', use: 'Base coat — robes and fabric', required: true },
            { name: 'Agrax Earthshade', use: 'Wash on robes and metal both', required: true },
            { name: 'Evil Sunz Scarlet', use: 'Layer on raised robe folds', required: true },
            { name: 'Leadbelcher', use: 'All metal and mechanical parts', required: true },
            { name: 'Nuln Oil', use: 'Wash on all metal surfaces', required: true },
            { name: 'Ironbreaker', use: 'Drybrush highlight on metal', required: true },
            { name: 'Tesseract Glow', use: 'Optical lenses and sensor eyes', required: true },
            { name: 'Corax White', use: 'Skull faces and bone details', required: false },
          ].map(paint => (
            <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class={`text-xs px-2 py-0.5 rounded mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 font-display ${paint.required ? 'bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113]' : 'border border-[#2a2a35] text-[#4a4855]'}`}>
                {paint.required ? 'Essential' : 'Optional'}
              </span>
              <div>
                <span class="text-sm font-semibold">{paint.name}</span>
                <span class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm"> — {paint.use}</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
        <p class="text-[#4a4855] text-sm mt-4 italic">~$45 for the full set. More paints than most factions — the detail count demands it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Cost breakdown -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-8">Honest cost breakdown</h2>
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
        {[
          { item: 'Combat Patrol: Adeptus Mechanicus', cost: '~$160', note: 'Manipulus, Vanguard/Rangers, Pteraxii, Serberys' },
          { item: 'Essential paints (7)', cost: '~$45', note: 'Spray + layer + 2 washes + 2 metals + glow' },
          { item: 'Basing supplies', cost: '~$12', note: 'Industrial/urban texture + rust tufts' },
          { item: 'Clippers + hobby knife', cost: '~$20', note: 'One-time purchase' },
          { item: 'Superglue', cost: '~$5', note: 'Fine multi-part models with small mechanical pieces' },
        ].map((row, i) => (
          <div class={`flex items-start justify-between px-5 py-4 gap-4 ${i % 2 === 0 ? '' : 'bg-[#111113]'}`}>
            <div>
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold">{row.item}</p>
              <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] mt-0.5">{row.note}</p>
            </div>
            <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] flex-shrink-0">{row.cost}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-5 py-4 bg-[#1f1d14] border-t border-[#c9a84c]">
          <p class="font-display font-semibold">All-in starter total</p>
